# Culligan reverse-engineering workspace.
#
# The shipped integration lives in ../ha-culligan-azure - this directory keeps
# only the diagnostic tooling. Everything the tooling PRODUCES is secret, so the
# ignores below are deliberately aggressive: it is far easier to un-ignore one
# file deliberately than to scrub a token out of git history.

# --- capture output: auth tokens, installation address, account/dealer IDs ---
mitm/capture/
*.jsonl
*.pcap
*.pcapng
api-summary.md

# --- private keys. The mitmproxy CA can sign a certificate for anything. ---
mitm/conf/
probe-certs/
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.crt
*.cer

# --- vendor binaries. Copyright, and large. ---
# Firmware images are vendor copyright and big. fw_extract.py writes its
# carved payloads next to them, so ignore the extraction output too.
firmware/
*.hdr
*.payload.bin
*.header.bin
*.extracted/
*.jffs2
# Probe output: contains the panel's real status history and its hostname.
tuxedo-probe-*.jsonl
tuxedo-decay*.jsonl
# Scratch artefacts from binary analysis (symbol caches etc).
syms.pkl
*.pkl
vmlinux.bin
mcu.bin
kernel.bin
apk/
*.apk
*.dex

# --- anything carrying personal data ---
dealer-email*
FINDINGS.md
*.creds
.env
*credentials*

# --- runtime noise ---
venv/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.log
probe-certs/
preview/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/

# --- OS ---
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store

# Agent and local files stay out of the repository.
.claude/
